CM_ BO_ 1792 "Request a single channel status block. Set ChannelNumber to 1..14.";
CM_ BO_ 1793 "Multiplexed 4-frame response on ChannelDataCANID + 1. FrameIndex selects the payload layout.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 FrameIndex "0 = status/core config, 1 = retry/inrush/input config, 2 = delayed-on/inrush/delayed-off flags, 3 = delayed-off time.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 ChannelName "Three uppercase letters packed into 16 bits as ((c0-'A') << 10) | ((c1-'A') << 5) | (c2-'A').";
CM_ BO_ 1808 "Digital input snapshot request. Payload is ignored by the controller.";
CM_ BO_ 1809 "Digital input snapshot response.";
CM_ SG_ 1809 DigitalInputMask "Bit 0 = DI1 through bit 7 = DI8. Set means the sampled input is logically high.";
CM_ BO_ 1810 "Request a single analogue input snapshot. Set InputNumber to 1..8.";
CM_ BO_ 1811 "Multiplexed 2-frame response on AnalogueInputDataCANID + 1. FrameIndex selects metadata or live value.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 FrameIndex "0 = input metadata and source voltage, 1 = converted live engineering value.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 Flags "Bit 0 = PullUpEnable, bit 1 = PullDownEnable, bit 2 = current logical digital state after pull-direction interpretation.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 ConvertedValue "Signed engineering value scaled by 1000. Interpret using the Units signal from frame 0.";
CM_ SG_ 1824 AliveCounter "Post-incrementing status counter. SystemStatus1 carries the pre-increment value.";
CM_ SG_ 1824 ECUVoltage "Battery voltage encoded as VBatt * 10.";
CM_ SG_ 1824 ErrorFlags "Bitmask: 0x0001 Overcurrent, 0x0002 Overtemp, 0x0004 Undervoltage, 0x0008 CRC check failed, 0x0010 SD card error, 0x0020 PC comms checksum error, 0x0040 GPS error, 0x0080 Temperature warning.";
CM_ SG_ 1825 AliveCounter "Second status frame uses the incremented counter value from SystemStatus1.";
CM_ BO_ 1840 "System configuration write message.";
CM_ SG_ 1840 WriteBitMask "Bits 0..6 gate bytes 0..6 respectively. Bit 0 = SystemCurrentLimit, bit 6 = MotionDeadTime.";
CM_ BO_ 1856 "Basic channel control message. Byte 1 is the only control byte used by firmware.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 ControlValue "0 disables the channel. Any non-zero value enables it. For CAN_PWM channels, the same byte is also taken as the PWM duty when the value is 100 or below.";
CM_ BO_ 1857 "Extended channel configuration write. Firmware reads byte 0 = ChannelNumber, byte 1 = ChannelType, bytes 2-3 = ChannelName, byte 4 = CurrentThresholdLow, byte 5 = CurrentThresholdHigh, byte 6 = RetryCount, byte 7 = WriteBitMask. Motorola start bits 23, 39, 47, and 55 therefore map to bytes 2, 4, 5, and 6 respectively.";
CM_ SG_ 1857 ChannelName "Three uppercase letters packed into 16 bits as ((c0-'A') << 10) | ((c1-'A') << 5) | (c2-'A').";
CM_ SG_ 1857 WriteBitMask "Bits 0,1,3,4,5 are implemented for ChannelType, ChannelName, CurrentThresholdLow, CurrentThresholdHigh, and RetryCount. Bit 2 is unused. Firmware also checks bit 6, but byte 7 is the mask itself, so use ChannelConfigF4 to set InrushCurrentThreshold.";
CM_ SG_ 1858 WriteBitMask "Bits 1 and 2 gate InrushDelay and ActiveHigh respectively. Bits 0 and 3 are unused.";
CM_ SG_ 1859 WriteBitMask "Bits 2 and 3 gate SoftStart and SoftStartTime respectively. Bits 0 and 1 are unused.";
CM_ BO_ 1860 "Dedicated inrush current threshold write message. Firmware reads byte 0 = ChannelNumber, byte 1 = InrushCurrentThreshold, byte 7 = WriteBitMask, and ignores bytes 2-6.";
CM_ SG_ 1860 WriteBitMask "Bit 0 gates InrushCurrentThreshold. When clear, the controller ignores byte 1. Bytes 2-6 are unused padding and should be sent as zero.";
CM_ BO_ 1861 "ChannelConfigF5 writes stored PWMSetDuty and Category. Only WriteBitMask bits 4 and 5 are implemented; bytes 1-4 remain reserved.";
CM_ BO_ 1862 "ChannelConfigF6 writes OnThreshold plus PWMMin/PWMMax for analogue/scaled channel modes.";
CM_ BO_ 1863 "ChannelConfigF7 writes OffThreshold, SoftStop, and delayed-on/off enable flags packed into DelayFlags.";
CM_ SG_ 1863 DelayFlags "Bit 0 = DelayedOn, bit 1 = DelayedOff.";
CM_ BO_ 1864 "ChannelConfigF8 writes ScaleMin and DelayedOffTrigger.";
CM_ BO_ 1865 "ChannelConfigF9 writes ScaleMax using bytes 1-4 as a raw big-endian IEEE-754 float.";
CM_ BO_ 1866 "ChannelConfigF10 writes SoftStopTime in milliseconds using bytes 1-4.";
CM_ BO_ 1867 "ChannelConfigF11 writes IntermittentOnTime in milliseconds using bytes 1-4.";
CM_ BO_ 1868 "ChannelConfigF12 writes IntermittentOffTime in milliseconds using bytes 1-4.";
CM_ BO_ 1869 "ChannelConfigF13 writes DelayedOnTime in milliseconds using bytes 1-4.";
CM_ BO_ 1870 "ChannelConfigF14 writes DelayedOffTime in milliseconds using bytes 1-4.";
CM_ BO_ 1871 "AnalogueConfigF0 writes analogue input flags, type, units, and calibration-point count.";
CM_ BO_ 1872 "AnalogueConfigF1 writes CalibrationVolt1 using bytes 1-4 as a raw big-endian IEEE-754 float.";
CM_ BO_ 1873 "AnalogueConfigF2 writes CalibrationValue1 using bytes 1-4 as a raw big-endian IEEE-754 float.";
CM_ BO_ 1874 "AnalogueConfigF3 writes CalibrationVolt2 using bytes 1-4 as a raw big-endian IEEE-754 float.";
CM_ BO_ 1875 "AnalogueConfigF4 writes CalibrationValue2 using bytes 1-4 as a raw big-endian IEEE-754 float.";
CM_ BO_ 1876 "AnalogueConfigF5 writes CalibrationVolt3 using bytes 1-4 as a raw big-endian IEEE-754 float.";
CM_ BO_ 1877 "AnalogueConfigF6 writes CalibrationValue3 using bytes 1-4 as a raw big-endian IEEE-754 float.";
CM_ BO_ 1878 "AnalogueConfigF7 writes NTCBeta using bytes 1-4 as a raw big-endian IEEE-754 float.";
CM_ BO_ 1879 "AnalogueConfigF8 writes NTCNominalResistance using bytes 1-4 as a raw big-endian IEEE-754 float.";
CM_ BO_ 1841 "SystemConfigF1 writes CAN termination and request CAN IDs not covered by SystemConfig.";
CM_ BO_ 1842 "SystemConfigF2 writes the remaining status/config CAN IDs.";
CM_ BO_ 1843 "SystemConfigF3 writes IMUwakeWindow in milliseconds using bytes 0-3.";
CM_ BO_ 1844 "SystemConfigF4 writes CANBusBitrate in bits per second using bytes 0-3. Firmware only accepts supported presets.";
CM_ BO_ 1845 "SystemConfigF5 carries TimeZoneRule bytes 0-7. Firmware buffers this frame until SystemConfigF6 arrives.";
CM_ BO_ 1846 "SystemConfigF6 carries TimeZoneRule bytes 8-14 in bytes 0-6. Firmware applies the packed rule once both timezone frames have arrived.";
CM_ SG_ 1841 WriteBitMask "Bit 0 gates CANResEnabled, bit 1 ChannelDataCANID, bit 2 DigitalInputDataCANID, bit 3 AnalogueInputDataCANID.";
CM_ SG_ 1842 WriteBitMask "Bit 0 gates SystemDataCANID, bit 1 ChannelConfigDataCANID, bit 2 SystemConfigDataCANID.";
CM_ SG_ 1843 WriteBitMask "Bit 0 gates IMUwakeWindow. Bytes 4-6 are unused padding and should be sent as zero.";
CM_ SG_ 1844 WriteBitMask "Bit 0 gates CANBusBitrate. Bytes 4-6 are unused padding and should be sent as zero.";
